hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1347","Abu Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Muhammad bin Yahya al-Quti’ told us, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yazid Al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “led the prayer of fear with them, and a line stood up.” In front of him, he lined up behind him, and he led those behind him in prayer, one rak’ah and two prostrations. Then they advanced until they took the place of their companions, and those came until They took their place, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led one rak’ah and two prostrations with them, then he saluted, and it was for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Two rak'ahs, and for them is one rak'ah.\""
"1348","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali bin Suwayd bin Manhouf narrated to us, Ruh narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, Al-Hakam and Mas’ar bin narrated to us. Kadam, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with something similar, and he did not say: “Then he greeted me.”"
"1349","Ahmad told us, Ruh told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Simmak al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar thing."
